  "high_value_council_tax_surcharge": {
   "definition_period": "year",
   "documentation": "Additional annual surcharge on owners of residential property in England worth at least \u00a32 million in 2026 prices. Owners, not occupiers, are liable, so the household is charged on its main residence only where it owns that home (owned outright or with a mortgage). Let property and second homes are not modelled. The annual OBR house-price index provides a proxy for converting simulated values to the 2026 valuation basis.",
